p.src:
The parallel with gravity is now exact rather than suggestive. A coordinate force is removable just as a curvilinear description of flat space is removable. Tidal acceleration is measured in general relativity by curvature. In later notation, neighboring freely falling worldlines satisfy the geodesic-deviation equation $\frac{D^2\xi^\mu}{D\tau^2}
 =-R^\mu{}_{\nu\rho\sigma}
   u^\nu\xi^\rho u^\sigma.$ Vanishing curvature means no invariant tidal field; nonzero curvature means that no coordinate choice can remove gravity throughout the region.

